From 4cc8004218a67e3317c63640a41ea31f76c08e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] video: rzg2l: load the boot logo from the rootfs
 partition

The splash image was loaded with

    ext4load mmc 0:1 0x48000000 boot_img_720p.bin.gz

but partition 1 of the RZ BSP image layout is the vfat "bootloader"
partition (meta-rz-bsp/wic/rz-image-bootpart-mmc.wks), so ext4load can
never mount it.  fs_set_blk_dev() finds the partition, fails to probe it
as ext4 and do_load() prints "Can't set block device"; the unzip that
follows then runs on whatever was left at 0x48000000 and prints "Error:
Bad gzipped data".  The LCDC is started regardless, so the panel comes up
scanning out uninitialised DRAM.

Read the image from partition 2 instead, out of /boot, where the BSP
environment already keeps Image and the device tree - one ext4 partition
then serves every file U-Boot reads, and the block cache is warm by the
time bootcmd loads the kernel.

Check both commands.  On failure blank the frame buffer and carry on
rather than returning early: the device tree declares the seamless
hand-over, so every kernel driver on the DRAM -> HDMI path skips its own
modeset, and a bootloader that leaves the LCDC off would cost the Weston
splash as well.  A blank screen plus a console warning is the least
surprising outcome.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G3L fast-boot logo, board specific]
---
 drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c b/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c
index ecbf6ec314..14bf08feaf 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@ static int adv7513_i2c_reg_write(struct udevice *dev, uint addr, uint mask, uint
 static int adv7513_i2c_reg_read(struct udevice *dev, uint8_t addr, uint8_t *data);
 
 int rzg2l_video_init(void){
+	int ret;
 
 	// adv7535_deinit();
 	rzg2l_cpg_init();
@@ -98,13 +99,35 @@ int rzg2l_video_init(void){
 	adv7535_init();
 #endif
 
-	/* Load image data for splash screen */
+	/*
+	 * Load the splash image.  It is installed in /boot on the rootfs
+	 * partition, next to Image and the device tree, so the same ext4
+	 * partition serves every file U-Boot reads.  Partition 1 is the vfat
+	 * "bootloader" partition of the BSP image layout and ext4load cannot
+	 * mount it.
+	 */
 #if (DISPLAY_MODE == MIPI_DSI_1080P)
-	run_command("ext4load mmc 0:1 0x48000000 boot_img_1080p.bin.gz",0);
+	ret = run_command("ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48000000 boot/boot_img_1080p.bin.gz", 0);
 #else
-	run_command("ext4load mmc 0:1 0x48000000 boot_img_720p.bin.gz",0);
+	ret = run_command("ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48000000 boot/boot_img_720p.bin.gz", 0);
 #endif
-	run_command("unzip 0x48000000 0x58000000",0);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = run_command("unzip 0x48000000 0x58000000", 0);
+
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * Start the pipeline anyway, on a blanked frame buffer.  The
+		 * device tree tells the kernel that the bootloader handed it a
+		 * running display and every driver on the path skips its own
+		 * modeset, so leaving the LCDC off here would cost the Weston
+		 * splash too - and scanning out uninitialised DRAM would put
+		 * noise on the screen instead of the missing logo.
+		 */
+		printf("fast-logo: no splash image, showing a blank screen\n");
+		memset((void *)(unsigned long)LCD_SRCM_ADDR, 0,
+		       LCD_SRCM_ADDR_OFFS);
+	}
+
 	dcache_disable();
 
 	// rzg2l_fpvcg_init();
